{"name":"Knight Elf","hex":"#926cac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young servant or follower; a trained military attendant in service of a lord.","A minor nobleman with an honourable military rank who had served as a page and squire."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confer knighthood upon.","To promote (a pawn) to a knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight"},{"term":"elf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being or spirit associated with illness, mischief, and harmful or dangerous magical influence; in later Norse sources, sometimes divided into benevolent light elves (inhabiting  Álfheimr) and malevolent dark elves.","A small, magical creature similar to a fairy, often mischievous, playful, or occasionally helpful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist into elflocks (of hair); to mat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knight","blocks":[{"text":"A knight is a person granted an honorary title of a knighthood by a head of state or representative for service to the monarch, the church, or the country, especially in a military capacity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg/330px-Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight","wikidata":"Q102083"},{"title":"Elf","blocks":[{"text":"An elf is a type of humanoid supernatural being in Germanic folklore. Elves appear especially in North Germanic mythology, being mentioned in the Icelandic Poetic Edda and the Prose Edda."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg/330px-%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.